  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Clans treat primeval stones as a resource that can found a settlement. The Gu Yue clan stayed on Qing Mao Mountain after finding a spirit spring in an underground cave, and that spring produces a large number of primeval stones as the village’s foundation.",
      "chapters": [
        4
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_gu_yue_clan",
        "loc_qing_mao_mountain"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Early narration shows them as oval, greyish white pieces that fit in a small bag.",
      "chapters": [
        9
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "form-and-two-uses",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "They measure the value of commodities, and they are also condensed matter of the world’s essence, usable on a Gu Master and important for cultivation.",
      "chapters": [
        8
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "form-and-two-uses",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_master"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Once someone is a Gu Master, they can extract primeval essence from a stone to replenish the primeval sea in the aperture. With enough stones, cultivation speed rises and a lower talent grade can be partly offset.",
      "chapters": [
        8
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "form-and-two-uses",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_primeval_sea"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "When a stone’s essence is fully retrieved, only powder remains.",
      "chapters": [
        50
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "form-and-two-uses",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Primeval stones are the driving force behind a Gu Master’s advancement. Without them, a Gu Master falls back on natural primeval essence recovery, which greatly slows cultivation. At the same time, without sufficient food, Gu worms starve.",
      "chapters": [
        91
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fuel-for-advancement",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_gu_worms"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Refining a Gu consumes a lot of primeval essence, so even family gifts of a few stones are framed as support for that first refinement.",
      "chapters": [
        9
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fuel-for-advancement",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "In practice the academy and the clan pay in stones. The first student to refine a vital Gu is promised twenty primeval stones,",
      "chapters": [
        7
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fuel-for-advancement",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "sys_vital_gu"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and weekly allowance comes as bags of stones for feeding Gu under financial pressure.",
      "chapters": [
        26
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fuel-for-advancement",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "During refinement itself, stones are the second way to refill a spent sea when natural recovery cannot keep up with a Gu’s resistance.",
      "chapters": [
        10
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "fuel-for-advancement",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    }
  ],
